  "id": "mirtazapine",
  "term": "mirtazapine",
  "definition": "Mirtazapine is a tetracyclic antidepressant that increases norepinephrine and serotonin release by blocking presynaptic alpha-2 adrenergic receptors. It also blocks certain serotonin receptors and strongly blocks histamine H1 receptors, and is used to treat depression and may also help with anxiety disorders.",
